  <data key="d8">..." where the relationship is between two entities. So in this case, the classifications (Other) and their point ranges (maybe as Financial_Metric) would have a relationship. But the point ranges are not standalone entities. Hmm, maybe the point ranges are part of the entity description, not separate entities. So the relationships would be between the classification (Other) and the severity index (Financial_Metric) or occurrence index (Financial_Metric). But the text doesn't explicitly state that. The first table links the classification with the point range and description. So perhaps each classification (Other) has a relationship with the point range (as a Financial_Metric) and the description (as part of the entity description). But the user's instructions say to extract relationships between entities. So if the point ranges are not entities, then the relationships would be between the classification (Other) and the severity index (Financial_Metric). Wait, the severity index is determined based on the classification. The text says "Chỉ số mức độ nghiêm trọng được xác định dựa trên mức độ ảnh hưởng của thiết bị..." So the severity index is linked to the classification. So the relationship would be between the classification (Other) and the severity index (Financial_Metric). Similarly, the occurrence index is linked to the probability indicators (like time between failures).</data>
